  "final_answer": "Converting the IUPAC Extended string 'α-D-Manp-(1→3)[α-D-Manp-(1→6)]-β-D-Manp-(1→4)-β-D-GlcpNAc-(1→4)-β-D-GlcpNAc-(1→4)-β-D-Glcp-(1→O)Cer' via GlycanFormatConverter yields the WURCS: WURCS=2.0/4,6,5/[a2122h-1b_1-5][a2122h-1b_1-5_2*NCC/3=O][a1122h-1b_1-5][a1122h-1a_1-5]/1-2-2-3-4-4/a4-b1_b4-c1_c4-d1_d3-e1_d6-f1. This encodes a 6-residue branched structure (two terminal α-Man, one β-Man, two β-GlcNAc, one β-Glc) with a ceramide (Cer) aglycone. Querying GlyTouCan with this WURCS returned 'Accession not found,' indicating the structure (including ceramide) is not registered in GlyTouCan, so no GlyTouCan accession maps to this WURCS. Thus the IUPAC representation is transformed into the linear WURCS sequence with explicit residue codes and linkage topology, but it lacks a corresponding GlyTouCan ID.",
